          "@value": "Barner Grass",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "Elephant grass (Pennisetum purpureum Schumach.) is a major tropical grass. It is one of the highest yielding tropical grasses. It is a very versatile species that can be grown under a wide range of conditions and systems: dry or wet conditions, smallholder or larger scale agriculture. It is a valuable forage and very popular throughout the tropics, notably in cut-and-carry systems (Mannetje, 1992; FAO, 2015). [Feedipedia]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:broader": {
        "@id": "urn:era-aom:livestock:AOM_000058"
      },
      "skos:relatedMatch": [
