      "era:conceptType": "legacy_aom_concept",
      "era:status": "unknown",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "Any measurable or observable characteristics related to the concentration of lignin (CHEBI:6457) in feed. Lignin is a complex organic polymer and a major structural component of plant cell walls. It provides rigidity and strength to plants, but in animal feeds, it is considered an anti-nutritional factor due to its indigestibility, reducing overall feed quality and nutrient availability. (HV GPT4)",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:broader": {
