      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "Gamba grass (Andropogon gayanus Kunth) is a perennial leafy grass of tropical Africa. Highly productive, drought- and fire-resistant grass, it forms dense stands used for pastures, hay and cut-and-carry systems. It is relished by livestock when young (before heading) and loses its nutritional value when it matures. [Feedipedia]",
        "@language": "en"
