      "era:status": "unknown",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "A biological treatment in which specific microorganisms (e.g., lactic acid bacteria, fungi, or enzymes) are intentionally introduced to feed materials to improve fermentation, preservation, or nutrient availability. Commonly used in silage production, composting, or enhancing digestibility of fibrous feeds.",
